  错综复杂 | cuò zōng fù zá | intricate and complex; tangled web
  千锤百炼 | qiān chuí bǎi liàn | hammered a thousand times; thoroughly tempered
  独具匠心 | dú jù jiàng xīn | possess unique ingenuity; original craftsmanship

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  结 | jié | tie knot; bind; crystallize; fruit | anudar; atar; cuajar; trabar | 纟 | silk / thread | 纟 (silk thread, knotting) | 吉 (jí, auspicious / firm) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: silk thread 纟 tied into an auspicious knot 吉, symbolizing binding structural elements firmly. | Weaving strong silk cords (纟) into an auspicious, unbreakable knot (吉) firmly binds components together (结). | Hebras de seda firme (纟) anudadas con ventura (吉) traban los elementos de un conjunto (结). | 35 | VMGR | 結
  构 | gòu | construct; build; compose; frame | construir; armar; urdir; tramar | 木 | tree / wood | 木 (timber beams) | 勾 (gōu, hook / interlocking joinery) | 8 | 左右结构 | Simplified from 構. Ancient pictogram of timber logs 木 interlocked using hooked joinery 勾 to build eaves. | Hooking timber beams (木) together with precision joints (勾) frames the skeleton of a building (构). | Ensamblar vigas de madera (木) con ganchos y espigas (勾) levanta el armazón de un edificio (构). | 51 | DPA | 構

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Tying cords together (结) to interlock sturdy wooden roof beams (构) assembles the overarching architecture and structure (结构).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Trabar ligaduras (结) que ensamblan las vigas maestras (构) levanta el armazón y la estructura (结构).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Chinese architectural theory (营造法式), 结构 specifically designated the dougong bracket sets (斗栱) and interlocking mortise-and-tenon timbers that distributed roof weight safely without nails. Metaphorically, it expanded into literary composition, sentence syntax, and macro-economics.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by falling 4th tone: 'jié gòu' (35-51). Rise smoothly on 'jié', then strike down firmly on 'gòu'.

